// B2 course (B1 → B2 roadmap), module 16 „B2 grammatika integratsioon” (b1b2-076…080), stage B2.
// Lesson template v4 (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12). One storyline, the cast a year after the B1 course
// (docs/COURSE_CAST.md), January–February, before Sofia's B2 exam (7 March) and before the café opens (18 April). Three
// people edit three texts. Tuul Logistika has tested a temporary warehouse in Ülenurme near Tartu since August; in early
// March the board decides whether a permanent warehouse opens there in May. Liis asked Sofia to edit the pilot's final
// report by the end of February; trainee Laura (until the end of February) wrote the draft (true facts, choppy
// sentences). Jaan and Kadri prepare the family café „Kohvik Mets” next to Nõmme market (opens 18 April; the name = the
// family name and Viktor's forest farm, where the bread recipe comes from; Muki is still the dog). A tasting evening for
// the neighbours in the unfinished café in February; Jaan writes „Meie lugu” and the house rules, Kadri edits them.
// Helgi proofreads by video call Oskar's (5.b) story for the school paper „Kase Kaja” (editor: class teacher Kristel
// Saar) about baking rye bread at Viktor's farm in January. One goal said on the first sheet: at the end the learner
// edits a real document together with its author (Sofia's report summary, 079 Kasuta) and writes its final version.
// Grammar (B2 integration, docs/METHODOLOGY_STANDARD.md §5): complex sentences and connectors (kuigi, ehkki, samal ajal
// kui, seetõttu, mistõttu, juhul kui) with the verb after them in 076; word order — verb second, a main clause after a
// subordinate one starts with the verb, given → new information, existential sentences with a partial subject, -ki/-gi
// (keegi, ükski, kunagi, isegi …-gi) in 077; participles -v / -tav / -nud / -tud as attributes, the des-form and
// nominalisation -mine / -ja (grammarPlan „nonfinite”) in 078; mood by function — impersonal for rules, conditional for
// requests and proposals, quotative for unchecked claims — in 079. Spiral: essive (projektijuhina, esindajana,
// personalitöötajana), translative (muutus tasuliseks, saada tõlkijaks, tihedaks), total vs partial object and subject
// (paigaldasid riiuleid / riiulid; Menüüs on suppe), all of them again in the final summary (079 Kasuta).
// Harno B2 formats: 4-option gap texts (076, 078, 079 Harjuta), a sentence bank (077 Harjuta), listening with short
// answers (076, 077, 078, 079), a debate with pro / contra cards and a decision and a semi-formal letter (076 Kasuta),
// a work-topic monologue (078 Kasuta), a summary of ~180 words (079 Kasuta).
// Module 15's words return (about 28 of its 45): allikas, väide, fakt, kontrollima, tõend, hinnang, oletus, kuulujutt,
// toon, rõhutama, kritiseerima, pealkiri, autor, arvamus, arutelu, argument, eesmärk, põhjendus, näide, kokkuvõte,
// järeldus, moonutama, võimalus, selguma, usaldusväärne, seisukoht, postitus, jagama.
//   076 Sofia's edited report chapter; Laura's introduction (option gaps), the project meeting (listening), Sofia's mail
//       to Liis; Kasuta: Liis offers Markus the logistician's job in the new Tartu warehouse from May — debate with
//       Sofia, phone call, reply letter.
//   077 Jaan reads his draft to Kadri (listening); Henri Pärtel's news item on the coming café (sentence bank, why it is
//       called Mets); Kasuta: the library's language café (in February; after the opening it meets at Kohvik Mets) —
//       three guests' stories (Tatjana, Daria, Aleksei), interview, the learner's story.
//   078 Oskar's story „Kuidas sünnib rukkileib”; Helgi and Oskar edit it by video call; Kasuta: Viktor's recipe cards,
//       Jaan explains the bread for the planned menu to cook Pille, a video for the café's site, a work instruction for the kitchen wall.
//   079 the café's house rules after the tasting evening (Jaan's draft, Kadri, a food-safety guide, guests' feedback); Sofia's report chapter on the paid car
//       park and her colleagues' voice messages; Kasuta: the module project — editor and author edit Laura's summary.
// Lesson 5 (080) is the module's check in Harno B2 form (unchanged). The v3 file is in archive/v3/b2/module16.js.
